{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfUdTvT5fZ6v4Kai9HPJT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"kind":"native_asset_criterion_assessment","criteria":[{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/evidence/source-faithfulness@5","disposition":"satisfied","rationale":"I recomputed the digests myself. All 18 source and candidate paths match the exact assessment basis, including candidate design/implementation-design.md at 2a5acf0f…. I then compared each of the seven candidate bodies with every stagePlan instruction in the full original declaration.\n\n- Conformance document: states the project pressure, lists all seven downstream surfaces and repeats the ABG ownership sentence word for word.\n- Implementation design: cites the conformance document as its authority, defines helloWorld() returning exactly \"Hello, world!\" and lists the seven separate surfaces, including an execution result that has no file.\n- package.json: private true and type module.\n- src/hello.mjs: a named export returning the exact string.\n- Test design: states both the component and the UAT obligation through the same export.\n- Both tests: use node:test and node:assert/strict, contain the exact import statement and assert by strict equality.\n- test-execution-plan.json: exact command and args, pass floor 2, \"fail 0\", and assertedReturnValue \"Hello, world!\".\n\nNo authored result file exists. I found no lost normative meaning.\n\nThe candidates also contain additions and narrowings. These are design-level choices that the source permits:\n- helloWorld is synchronous, with no imports and no default export.\n- package.json has exactly two keys.\n- Each test file declares exactly one test.\n- The conformance document declares no stdout, CLI, HTTP, UI or deployment surface. This follows from expectedStdout null and predecessor requirement-candidate:03.\n- The conformance document adds a qualifier after the ABG sentence: it grants no authority and places no machinery in the subject.\n- The plan carries an extra derivedFrom field.\n\nTwo departures from the literal source wording are disclosed and not repaired:\n- The test design names the full files as its evidence source, where the source says \"artifact summaries\" (req-pressure:03 is still pending).\n- The comment at the top of the component test names its predecessors but leaves out package.json.","evidence":[{"path":"original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt","quote":"package.json must be private:true and type:module."},{"path":"package.json","quote":"\"private\": true"},{"path":"original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt","quote":"Import the named export exactly as: import { helloWorld } from"},{"path":"test/component/hello.test.mjs","quote":"import { helloWorld } from \"../../src/hello.mjs\";"},{"path":"specification/project-conformance.md","quote":"ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence."},{"path":"specification/project-conformance.md","quote":"This sentence describes the environment that builds the subject. It grants no"},{"path":"design/implementation-design.md","quote":"Authority: specification/project-conformance.md"},{"path":"original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt","quote":"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"path":"design/test-design.md","quote":"Evidence source: package.json and src/hello.mjs"},{"path":"test-execution-plan.json","quote":"\"expectedStdoutMatch\": \"fail 0\""},{"path":"src/hello.mjs","quote":"return \"Hello, world!\";"}]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/evidence/modality-and-conflicts@5","disposition":"satisfied","rationale":"The conflicting source meaning is kept as source and is not enacted. This covers the stagePlan per-vector write limits, executeFromPlan and the witness parity rule. None of the candidates carries a stage vector, a traversal controller, a ledger or odd_sdlc machinery. The parity rule's ban on copying agrees with the current boundary, and inventory verification observed no copied machinery.\n\nThe other modalities are also kept:\n- Supporting: the witness remains unverified provenance.\n- Speculative: the source anticipates depth coverage. The test design fixes exactly one test per file, but the plan keeps a pass floor and does not pin a pass count, so the speculative allowance survives in the plan.\n\nNo owner ruling exists in the admitted material, and no candidate claims one.\n\nOpen pressures remain open. They are either still pending in stage-2 or disclosed again in the author report:\n- req-pressure:03, 04, 05, 07, 09, 12, 15, 17, 18 and 19.\n\nSome pressures were settled by design choice without an owner ruling. The design picked no extra package fields, a synchronous return and exactly one test per file. These choices sit within what the source permits, so they narrow rather than weaken. They are recorded as residuals below so they stay visible.\n\nThe author report does not repeat the conflicting pressures req-pressure:01 and 02 or the witness pressure 16. They remain recorded in the stage assets and are carried as outside residuals.","evidence":[{"path":"original-js-sdlc-bootstrap-declaration.txt","quote":"do not copy odd_sdlc runtime code, ledgers, phase-flow controller, or local truth surfaces"},{"path":"semantic-assets/stage-0.json","quote":"This asset keeps the artifact set, each artifact's content obligation, the derivation order and the acceptance rule as source meaning."},{"path":"semantic-assets/stage-0.json","quote":"The source anticipates, without requiring, that the generated tests may add depth coverage"},{"path":"design/test-design.md","quote":"Each file declares exactly one test through test()."},{"path":"design/implementation-design.md","quote":"declares no other field, so it adds no bin, script or other output surface."},{"path":"origina